# SimuCell3D 1.0 documentation (archived)

:::{important}
These pages are the documentation of release 1.0, re-rendered as it was written in 2024. They
have not been updated. For the current release, read the
**[current documentation]({{SITE}}stable/)**.
:::

## This release

Release
: SimuCell3D 1.0, the code published with the article

Authors
: Steve Runser, Roman Vetter and Dagmar Iber (Iber Lab, ETH Zurich)

Tag
: `v1.0`, commit `38af451`, 26 June 2024

Zenodo archive cited by the article
: [doi:10.5281/zenodo.10796908](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10796908), commit `5342bf8`, 8 March 2024

Article
: Runser, S., Vetter, R. & Iber, D. SimuCell3D: three-dimensional simulation of tissue mechanics with cell polarization. *Nat. Comput. Sci.* **4**, 299-309 (2024). [doi:10.1038/s43588-024-00620-9](https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-024-00620-9)

Original repository
: [git.bsse.ethz.ch/iber/Publications/2024_runser_simucell3d](https://git.bsse.ethz.ch/iber/Publications/2024_runser_simucell3d)

The pages below are the `README.md` and the `doc/` folder of tag `v1.0`, plus the README files
under `scripts/` and `src/mesh/`. They were written by Steve Runser as part of the release. The
documentation files are the same in the Zenodo archive and in the tag. At the time the project
was called DCM.

Use 1.0 to reproduce or compare with the figures of the article. Later releases change
simulation results; the
[release notes of 1.0]({{SITE}}stable/whats_new/v1.0.html)
compare the two 1.0 snapshots, and the
[release notes of 2.1]({{SITE}}stable/whats_new/v2.1.html) list
what changed since 1.0, including defects of 1.0 found later.

## Obtaining and building 1.0

The tag is in the repository of the 2.x releases:

```console
$ git clone https://github.com/nilesh-patil/simucell3d.git
$ cd simucell3d
$ git checkout v1.0      # the tag; or: git checkout 5342bf8 for the archived commit
```

Build from the repository root. Release 1.0 needs a C++17 compiler with OpenMP and CMake; it
declares `cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.0)`, which CMake 3.x accepts with a deprecation
warning and CMake 4 refuses. With CMake 4, add `-DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5` to the
`cmake` line.

```console
$ sed -i 's|/data/input_meshes/fig_3_vesicle_triangulated.vtk|data/input_meshes/fig_3_vesicle.vtk|' parameters_vesicle.xml
$ mkdir build
$ cd build
$ cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ..
$ make -j4
$ ./simucell3d ../parameters_vesicle.xml
```

The executable takes one argument, the parameter file. The parameter files are in the
repository root. Each one names, in a comment at its top, the compile-time settings it needs in
`include/global_configuration.hpp`. `parameters_vesicle.xml` needs `POLARIZATION_MODE_INDEX 1`,
`CONTACT_MODEL_INDEX 2` and `DYNAMIC_MODEL_INDEX 0`, which are the defaults of the tag, so a
default build runs it.

:::{note}
The `sed` line is needed because `parameters_vesicle.xml` of the tag names the input mesh
`/data/input_meshes/fig_3_vesicle_triangulated.vtk`, which is not in the tag; without it the run
stops at once with "input mesh file ... not found". Other files need a different build:
`parameters_default_dynamic.xml`, for example, is written for `CONTACT_MODEL_INDEX 1`, the default
of the archived commit `5342bf8` but not of the tag. Change the setting in
`include/global_configuration.hpp` and rebuild before you run such a file.
:::

